# Agent Integration — Final Wiring Steps

You now have **everything** needed to run the agent pipeline end-to-end. This
document walks through the last 20 minutes of setup to get `Open WhatsApp`
actually working from a debug screen.

---

## 1. Gradle dependencies (`app/build.gradle.kts`)

Add these if they're not already present. Most Amar Vault projects already
have kotlinx-serialization and Hilt — verify before adding.

```kotlin
plugins {
    kotlin("plugin.serialization") version "<your kotlin version>"
    id("com.google.dagger.hilt.android")
    id("com.google.devtools.ksp")
}

dependencies {
    // kotlinx.serialization — DSL uses this
    implementation("org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-serialization-json:1.6.3")

    // Room — checkpoint persistence
    implementation("androidx.room:room-runtime:2.6.1")
    implementation("androidx.room:room-ktx:2.6.1")
    ksp("androidx.room:room-compiler:2.6.1")

    // Hilt
    implementation("com.google.dagger:hilt-android:2.51")
    ksp("com.google.dagger:hilt-android-compiler:2.51")
    implementation("androidx.hilt:hilt-navigation-compose:1.2.0")

    // Compose (debug screen only)
    implementation("androidx.compose.material3:material3:1.2.1")
    implementation("androidx.lifecycle:lifecycle-viewmodel-compose:2.7.0")
    implementation("androidx.compose.runtime:runtime-livedata:1.6.3")
}
```

