## 5. `VaultApplication.kt` (or your existing Application class)

**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT call `AgentStateHolder.init(...)` here. The Hilt module
handles initialization lazily on first `SnapshotCache` injection, which avoids
a race with the Hilt graph.

If you have no existing `Application` class, create one:

```kotlin
package com.amar.vault

import android.app.Application
import dagger.hilt.android.HiltAndroidApp

@HiltAndroidApp
class VaultApplication : Application() {
    override fun onCreate() {
        super.onCreate()
        // Agent wiring is handled by AgentModule.
        // Do NOT call AgentStateHolder.init() here — the module does it.
    }
}
```

And reference it from manifest:

```xml
<application
    android:name=".VaultApplication"
    ...>
```

